      "writtenOn": "2026-07-07T23:26:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Is PD_HARD_RESET happens for self powered devices also ?\n\nNo, `dpm_check_tbt_usb4_reset` is only called in the first while loop of `pdc_dpm_balance_source_ports`. This is when the DPM is processing max current request set by `sink_max_pdo_requested`. This will only be set when the port is a PD source.\n\n\u003e  Is there any possibility of allocating 3A for the power role swap request ?\n\nIf this is referring to FR swap, it will allocate 3A through a different path (setting `source_frs_max_requested`). That caused the second while loop in `pdc_dpm_balance_source_ports` to process the request so there will not be a TBT/USB4 check and hard reset after allocating 3A for FRS.\n\nFor a power role swap, that would cause the PDC power manager to go back through the PD Source States which would cause the PDC DPM to potentially offer 5V/3A triggering a reset. Same as hotplug.",
      "parentUuid": "a7184871_68a6d8eb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "df1aef2a4a9fa00ec07a743442a00263f62aa68a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90748683_04d8b32e",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 77,
